      "thinking": "Nubemhat, queen in the 17th dynasty and wife of Sobekemsaf, has a name meaning \"gold in front\" — Nbw-m-ḥꜣ.t. I'm checking whether the transliteration uses a plain h or the emphatic ḥ, since that changes the reading between \"Neb-em-het\" and the gold-themed version.\n\nTesting candidate Nb-mḥy.t, \"Lord/Lady is Mehyt\" — the consonants n,b,m,ḥ,t do line up, but this points to a goddess name rather than the \"gold\" word, so it's a different etymology and I should exclude it. I'm also starting to check Nb=j-m-jꜥḥ as another possibility, which would need a ḥ following the ꜥ.\n\n",
