      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Nubemhat\", \"choices\": [], \"reasoning\": \"Record 1, Nubemhat, reads as Nbw-m-ḥꜣ.t, 'gold is in front': nbw 'gold', the preposition m, and ḥꜣ.t 'front'. C1 (Nb-m-ht, 'Neb-em-het'): its consonants n-b-m-h-t fit the spelling, but the transliteration has nb without w and the translation gives 'Neb', so its first word is nb 'lord/all', not nbw 'gold'. Its last word is ht with plain h, not ḥꜣ.t 'front'. Different words, so a different name. C2 (Nb-mḥy.t, 'Neb-mehyt', 'the lord/lady is Mehyt'): the consonants n-b-m-ḥ-(y)-t could fit, but the words are nb plus the goddess name Mḥy.t, not nbw 'gold' plus m ḥꜣ.t 'in front'. Different words. C3 (Nb=j-m-jꜥḥ, 'Nebi-em-jah', 'my lord is the moon'): it has no t, so the final t of Nubemhat would render a consonant the candidate lacks. Its words (nb=j, m, jꜥḥ 'moon') also differ. No match.\"}"
